iption":"","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2026-08-12/doc-inimynsi4367466.shtml","time":"2026-08-11T16:00:00.000Z","tags":["芯片/半导体"]},{"source":"新浪科技","sourceColor":"#e6162d","title":"追光聚海 新快报青年文艺英才计划今日启动","description":"","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2026-08-12/doc-inimynsc4035092.shtml","time":"2026-08-11T16:00:00.000Z","tags":[]},{"source":"新浪科技","sourceColor":"#e6162d","title":"定价直接突破1万元！iPhone 18 Pro维持256GB起步：成苹果史上最贵Pro","description":"","url":"https://finance.sina.com.cn/tech/roll/2026-08-12/doc-inimynrz7263625.shtml","time":"2026-08-11T16:00:00.000Z","tags":["手机","大公司"]},{"source":"Dev.to","sourceColor":"#4b3e99","title":"A Little Briny - A Multi-Agent Writing Experiment","description":"All of the text below the dividing line here was generated by a group of AI agents, using the \"Discussion\" tool I described here. This particular story used six personas: Joran, Ismere, Nico, Faye, Thomas, and Mem. Mem in particular had an impact I wasn't expecting: it was intended to push the story more towards an AI-generated tone, but I think it wound up having the opposite effect. In an attempt to trim excess words for efficiency I think Mem wound up also trimming some of the flourishes that signal AI generated text. Just for fun I've been running this text through several \"AI Detectors\"; the results are all over the map (perhaps unsurprisingly). I'll include both the details of the personas and some of the AI detection results in future posts (along with the subsequent chapters of the","url":"https://dev.to/cberube_5/a-little-briny-a-multi-agent-writing-experiment-4c8h","time":"2026-08-11T16:00:00.000Z","tags":["人工智能","手机","芯片/半导体"]},{"source":"Dev.to","sourceColor":"#4b3e99","title":"Beyond Syntax: Why Design Thinking is the Secret Sauce of Great Frontend Engineering","description":"We often focus on the \"how\" of coding—which framework to use, how to optimize bundle size, or the latest CSS trick. But, in my experience at the intersection of architecture and software engineering, the real power lies in the \"why.\" Design thinking isn't just for UX designers; it’s a critical tool for frontend engineers. It’s the shift from \"How can I build this feature?\" to \"How does this feature serve the user’s journey within our digital ecosystem?\" As an architect, I learned that a building is never just a collection of walls. It’s a solution to human movement, light, and purpose. Applying this to Frontend: Components as Spaces: When I build a component in React, I think of it as a defined space. Is it breathable? Does it have a clear purpose? Does it guide the user efficiently? Empat","url":"https://dev.to/mahtab_ashrafi_645b08e6c4/beyond-syntax-why-design-thinking-is-the-secret-sauce-of-great-frontend-engineering-51hc","time":"2026-08-11T15:59:51.000Z","tags":["软件应用","科技创投","智能硬件"]},{"source":"芯片半导体","sourceColor":"#004d40","title":"午间头条：英伟达正开发雄心勃勃的开源AI模型；英特尔将股票发行规模上调至$200亿 - Moomoo","description":"","url":"https://www.moomoo.com/hans/news/post/74503683/top-midday-stories-nvidia-developing-ambitious-open-source-ai-model","time":"2026-08-11T15:58:07.000Z","tags":["人工智能","芯片/半导体","软件应用"],"topic":true},{"source":"Dev.to","sourceColor":"#4b3e99","title":"Nine ways to talk to a local model","description":"A nine-tool survey of local-model interfaces on one GPU: what worked, what silently failed, and Nine pieces of software for talking to a local model went through this machine over about two The spread in outcomes was enormous, and almost none of it was about the model. The same weights Here is what each one was actually good at. Tool Good at The number that mattered Ollama the default, broadly reliable 32.9 t/s gen on a 30B MoE llama.cpp fastest, once tuned 27.1 t/s vs Ollama's 23.4 LM Studio document extraction to file 10 rows, exact match, no invented values little-coder small-model coding harness 8/8 in 2.1 min, then a version bump broke it Unsloth Studio fastest single-file result unusable past a 4096-toke